# No custom CSS

Streamlit UI must use stock widgets + theme TOML only. No injected CSS/HTML chrome.

## Forbidden in `src/happy_housing/app/`

- `<style>` blocks for colours, fonts, cards, or general look-and-feel
- Inline `style="..."` attributes
- `unsafe_allow_html=True` for styling (except the layout-density helper below)
- `st.html(...)` / raw HTML markup used only for look-and-feel
- Custom CSS files, class-based skinning (`hh-*` layout classes, etc.)

## Allowed

- Theme tokens in `.streamlit/config.toml` (`[theme]`, fonts, chart colours)
- Streamlit widgets: `st.title`, `st.metric`, `st.tabs`, `st.markdown` (GFM only — bold, strikethrough, links)
- Map/deck.gl layer colours and Altair/plot encodings (data viz, not page CSS)
- **One layout-density exception:** `apply_dense_top_layout()` may set main
  `block-container` / `stMainBlockContainer` `padding-top` only. Streamlit has no
  TOML knob for the large gap under top `st.navigation`. Do not extend this to
  colours, fonts, sidebars, or widget chrome.

## Prefer

| Need | Use |
|---|---|
| Brand / page title | `st.title` / `st.header` (skip on pages already labeled by top nav) |
| KPIs | `st.metric` (+ `delta` / `delta_color`) |
| Emphasis / strike | Markdown (`**bold**`, `~~strike~~`) |
| Layout | `st.columns`, `st.container`, `st.tabs` |
| Look & feel | `.streamlit/config.toml` only |

If a design seems to need custom CSS beyond the padding-top exception above,
change the design to fit Streamlit — do not inject more CSS.
